\paragraph{Baseline scaling.} Prompting baselines exhibit a mixed pattern at 14B. In the 3-shot setting, Qwen3-14B (73.12\%) outperforms Qwen3-8B (68.78\%) by 4.34\pp{}, consistent with the expected benefit of increased capacity for in-context learning. In contrast, 14B 0-shot accuracy (66.24\%) falls 2.46\pp{} below 8B (68.70\%); this reversal may reflect differences in instruction tuning between the two model sizes rather than a capacity limitation, and we do not draw strong conclusions from it. Regardless of prompting strategy, the best prompting result (14B 3-shot, 73.12\%) remains 16.82\pp{} below fine-tuned \cls{} at 8B (89.94\%, Table~\ref{tab:main_results}), confirming that model scaling alone does not substitute for task-specific fine-tuning at function level.

